    Small negatives appear in BOTH because a Beta(0.5,0.5) prior and
    clipping are applied to theta, so the M-step maximises the
    posterior while the printed quantity is the plain likelihood.
    What matters is that C-chain is no worse than B-pool: the exact
    (pi_1, A) M-step introduces no additional non-monotonicity.

